# Cloudflare Pages serves assets with a four-hour cache by default, which is
# how a redeploy became invisible to anyone who had already loaded the page —
# the HTML revalidated and asked for the new stylesheet, but the browser kept
# serving the old one from cache.
#
# The rule here: HTML always revalidates, assets are cached but every asset that
# can change carries a version. style.css is versioned by query string
# (?v=N — bump it when you edit the file); the icons are versioned by filename.
# Changing an asset without changing how it is addressed will strand returning
# visitors on the old one for a day.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
